# Primary Buttons Use Filled Icons

A **primary button** is any solid brand-blue control (`background: var(--primary)`,
white label/icon) — full-size CTAs, icon-only circles, and solid-blue chips.
Its icon is always the **filled** twin. This is a permanent, non-negotiable
design rule.

Applies everywhere that control appears: login, admin, marketing, send, and
intent / reply chips that use the primary (solid blue) treatment.

## What counts

- `.btn-primary`, `.adm-btn--primary`, `.adm-icon-btn--primary`,
  `.pf-btn--primary`, `.dash-btn--primary`, `.mkt-btn-primary`,
  `.cmp-tool-btn--primary`, `.gv-btn--primary`, `.wmod-btn--primary`,
  `.vf-modal-btn--primary`, `.demo-btn.primary`
- `.chip.chip-primary`, selected solid-blue chips (`.ms-chip.is-selected`)
- `.sc-send` (the composer send circle)

Ghost, outline, tinted, and welcome intent chips (`.ws-intent-chip`,
`.chip-dive`, `.btn-ghost`) stay **outlined** (`FILL` 0).

## How to fill

Material Symbols: `font-variation-settings: 'FILL' 1, 'wght' 400, 'GRAD' 0, 'opsz' 24`.
The SVG shim (`js/icon-svg-shim.js`) reads that and swaps in the filled twin.
Do not pick an `*_outline` / `*_border` ligature on a primary button — use the
filled sibling (`help` not `help_outline`, `star` not `star_outline`).

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: solid blue button, outline icon -->
<button class="btn btn-primary">
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined">login</span>Sign in
</button>
<!-- (default FILL 0, or an *_outline ligature) -->

<!-- ✅ GOOD: same button, filled icon -->
<button class="btn btn-primary">
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined">login</span>Sign in
</button>
```

```css
.btn-primary .material-symbols-outlined,
.chip.chip-primary .material-symbols-outlined {
  font-variation-settings: 'FILL' 1, 'wght' 400, 'GRAD' 0, 'opsz' 24;
}
```

## Rules for the agent

- When adding or editing a primary (solid blue) button or chip, set the icon
  to filled. Prefer the shared CSS hook already in `wise.css` / `auth.css` /
  `marketing.css` / `wiseai-chat.css` — do not invent a parallel fill system.
- When promoting a chip to `chip-primary` (or any `--primary` / `btn-primary`
  class), do not leave the icon outlined.
- Do not fill icons on ghost, outline, or tinted chips just because they sit
  next to a primary control.
